---
import BaseHead from '../components/BaseHead.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
	<head>
		<BaseHead
			title="Writing | Ravikumar Buragapu"
			description="Technical writing by Ravikumar Buragapu on production AI, agentic systems, platform engineering, developer productivity, and enterprise engineering."
		/>
	</head>
	<body>
		<Header />
		<main>
			<header>
				<h1>Writing</h1>
				<p>
					I write about the engineering decisions that determine whether
					emerging technologies work reliably in the real world—from
					building productive engineering platforms to operating
					secure, observable, and accountable AI systems in production.
				</p>
				<p>
					My writing combines architecture, engineering practice,
					and operational experience, with a focus on turning
					technical ideas into systems that work at scale.
				</p>
			</header>

			<section aria-labelledby="production-ai">
				<h2>AI systems in production</h2>
				<p>
					As AI systems move from generating responses to taking
					actions, engineering discipline becomes essential.
					These articles explore evaluation, identity, permissions,
					operational controls, and the boundaries of agent autonomy.
				</p>

				<article>
					<h3>
						<a href="/blog/hard-part-of-agents">
							The Hard Part of Agents Isn't the Model
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						Why the hardest challenges in agentic AI often lie
						outside the model—in identity, authorization,
						observability, execution controls, and operational
						accountability.
					</p>
					<p><a href="/blog/hard-part-of-agents">Read article</a></p>
				</article>

				<article>
					<h3>
						<a href="/blog/earning-agentic-autonomy">
							Earning Agentic Autonomy: An Eval Architecture for AI Agents
						</a>
					</h3>
					<p>
						How evaluation evidence, explicit decision criteria,
						and runtime enforcement can help determine when an
						AI agent is ready to act with greater autonomy.
					</p>
					<p>
						<a href="/blog/earning-agentic-autonomy">Read article</a>
					</p>
				</article>
			</section>

			<section aria-labelledby="platform-engineering">
